WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.899 --> 00:00:09.000
There they are. There they are! I see them. Right, Clemont?

2
00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:14.000
Absolutely. Go ahead, Dedenne. You, too, Pikachu.

3
00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:17.400
- Na-na-na!
- Pika!

4
00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:21.800
- Pika!
- Wow.

5
00:00:21.866 --> 00:00:24.333
- It’s like an electric shower.
- Awesome.

6
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.099
- And Pikachu and Dedenne are loving it.
- I know. Right?

7
00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:31.000
My big brother invented these all by himself.

8
00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:32.400
- Ah!
- Wow, you did?

9
00:00:32.466 --> 00:00:35.466
Yeah, I call them Clemontic Showers.

10
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.966
The place hasn’t changed a bit. It takes me back.

11
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:44.166
- Clemont?
- Huh?

12
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:46.233
It’s really you, Clemont.

13
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.900
Ms. Éclairisse, it’s been so long.

14
00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:52.333
- Huh? Who’s that?
- Huh? What’s going on?

15
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.933
- Pi! Pika!
- Huh!

16
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.833
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

17
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.566
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

18
00:01:01.766 --> 00:01:04.233
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

19
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.300
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

20
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:10.366
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

21
00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:13.633
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

22
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.000
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

23
00:01:17.066 --> 00:01:19.433
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

24
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

25
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

26
00:01:34.866 --> 00:01:38.633
As our heroes continue their journey to the Coumarine City Gym,

27
00:01:38.699 --> 00:01:42.733
they have unexpectedly crossed paths with a woman named Éclairisse.

28
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.199
You see, right now I’m on a journey with my little sister and my friends.

29
00:01:47.266 --> 00:01:48.966
That’s wonderful.

30
00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:52.166
Hi. My name’s Ash and this is my partner, Pikachu.

31
00:01:52.233 --> 00:01:54.933
- Pikachu.
- Hi. Nice to meet you. I'm Serena.

32
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.699
Hi. I’m the little sister. My name’s Bonnie.

33
00:01:57.766 --> 00:02:00.933
- Dedenne, say hi to the lady.
- Na-na!

34
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.199
Bonnie. Clemont has told me how cute and sweet you are.

35
00:02:04.266 --> 00:02:06.433
It’s such a pleasure to finally meet you.

36
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.000
And Clemont’s told me a lot about you.

37
00:02:09.066 --> 00:02:12.433
Always saying how pretty and how nice Ms. Éclairisse is.

38
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.433
I think he really, really likes you!

39
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.333
You’re a keeper, so please take care of my brother.

40
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.533
- Ah!
- I’m a keeper?

41
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.500
Right. You’d be perfect for him ‘cause you’re so smart.

42
00:02:22.566 --> 00:02:26.966
- Uh! What?
- I told you to stop this a million times.

43
00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:30.299
I was just trying to help you. Come on.

44
00:02:30.366 --> 00:02:32.299
But I don’t need that kind of help!

45
00:02:32.366 --> 00:02:35.766
- Come on, Clemont, please?

46
00:02:37.366 --> 00:02:40.033
A school for studying Electric-type Pokémon?

47
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.033
Pika! Pika?

48
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:45.433
Yeah. It’s in the middle of town. See, Clemont was a student there.

49
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.433
- Wow, no joke?
- Nope. Look. There it is.

50
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.566
Would you all like to come have a look?

51
00:02:50.633 --> 00:02:53.799
- Cool. Is that okay?
- Of course it is.

52
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.966
-Pika!

53
00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:07.600
Here at our school, Trainers travel from all over to learn

54
00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:10.566
everything they can about Electric-type Pokémon.

55
00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:15.166
Our students specialize in researching the biology

56
00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:17.833
and behaviors of Electric-type Pokémon.

57
00:03:17.899 --> 00:03:21.033
Their studies extend to Pokémon of other types as well.

58
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.866
As part of this research, they learn all about

59
00:03:23.933 --> 00:03:28.566
how people and Pokémon can and should coexist in harmony.

60
00:03:31.066 --> 00:03:34.200
Many great Trainers have gone on to be very successful

61
00:03:34.266 --> 00:03:39.333
after leaving this school, but Clemont is one of the most notable graduates of all.

62
00:03:39.399 --> 00:03:42.233
Come on. I think you’re exaggerating a bit.

63
00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:45.666
No way. You’re amazing. Yup. You keep coming up with

64
00:03:45.733 --> 00:03:49.833
these totally incredible inventions that always blow up in the end.

65
00:03:51.266 --> 00:03:55.600
They call you the Electric-type Whiz Kid all around Lumiose City, don’t they?

66
00:03:55.666 --> 00:03:59.733
- I know your father calls you that, too.
- Your father?

67
00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:02.533
That’s Meyer, right?

68
00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.566
You see, it was my father who told me I needed to go to this school.

69
00:04:06.633 --> 00:04:09.700
"Meet lots of Pokémon Trainers and make lots of friends.

70
00:04:09.766 --> 00:04:11.933
Study hard and broaden your horizons.”

71
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.299
He told me to do that and off I went.

72
00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:17.666
So how did it work out? Did you make lots of friends?

73
00:04:17.733 --> 00:04:18.800
Pika! Pikachu?

74
00:04:18.866 --> 00:04:23.266
Mm-hm. I made friends with all kinds of great students and Pokémon, too,

75
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:26.633
but all that studying and the research was tough, to say the least.

76
00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.700
The curriculum here is quite rigorous.

77
00:04:28.766 --> 00:04:31.800
It’s a challenge to do the work and make it all the way to graduation.

78
00:04:31.866 --> 00:04:35.366
Yes and my graduation research was particularly tough.

79
00:04:35.433 --> 00:04:37.266
Graduation research?

80
00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:40.000
I studied the power of Electric-type Pokémon

81
00:04:40.066 --> 00:04:43.099
and how the power of science can build the future.

82
00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:44.800
That was my major focus.

83
00:04:44.866 --> 00:04:47.166
I recall you did struggle with that.

84
00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:49.500
You said you couldn’t come up with any good topics.

85
00:04:49.566 --> 00:04:53.300
Right. So I used to go for walks to try to clear my mind.

86
00:04:53.366 --> 00:04:55.400
That’s when I met you-know-who.

87
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.566
-Huh?

88
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.000
- A Shinx.
- Shinx!

89
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:10.966
Oh, yeah, the Pokémon Center.

90
00:05:13.099 --> 00:05:16.900
Thanks so much for waiting. This Shinx was completely exhausted,

91
00:05:16.966 --> 00:05:19.633
so it took an exceptional amount of time to recover.

92
00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.933
- Shinx! Shinx! Shinx!
- Ah. What a relief.

93
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.599
I’ve seen this more times than I can count.

94
00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:28.866
It appears to have something to do with the local environment.

95
00:05:28.933 --> 00:05:31.700
If only there were a place where these Pokémon

96
00:05:31.766 --> 00:05:33.933
could easily absorb electrical energy.

97
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.099
A place where they can easily absorb electrical energy.

98
00:05:38.166 --> 00:05:41.900
That’s it! I’ve come up with a great idea, Shinx.

99
00:05:41.966 --> 00:05:43.966
-Shinx.

100
00:05:44.966 --> 00:05:48.200
I’ll collect the power generated by the school’s Pokémon,

101
00:05:48.266 --> 00:05:51.633
store it in battery, send it by cables throughout the town

102
00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.300
and make an electricity shower for Electric types.

103
00:05:54.366 --> 00:05:56.900
I’ll call it the Clemontic Shower.

104
00:05:56.966 --> 00:05:59.500
I can just see it!

105
00:05:59.566 --> 00:06:02.166
The future is now, thanks to science.

106
00:06:02.233 --> 00:06:04.700
-Huh?

107
00:06:04.766 --> 00:06:07.300
Shinx!

108
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.700
Here. See this? With my new system,

109
00:06:12.766 --> 00:06:16.866
you’ll be able to absorb all that electricity I know you love so much.

110
00:06:16.933 --> 00:06:18.033
Shinx! Shinx!

111
00:06:18.099 --> 00:06:21.233
I want to make a town where Electric types can live happily.

112
00:06:21.299 --> 00:06:24.133
No, a world where all Pokémon can live happily.

113
00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.366
That would be my dream come true.

114
00:06:26.433 --> 00:06:29.566
Shinx, you’d live there, now, wouldn’t you?

115
00:06:29.633 --> 00:06:31.500
- Huh?
- Shinx! Shinx!

116
00:06:34.099 --> 00:06:37.466
That’s how I completed my graduate research project.

117
00:06:37.533 --> 00:06:40.733
The electrical transmission system that Clemont invented

118
00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:43.266
was well received not only by the school,

119
00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:46.700
but by the entire town’s population as well.

120
00:06:48.433 --> 00:06:50.066
What a great story.

121
00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:54.233
That’s the very first time I heard Clement talk about Shinx.

122
00:06:54.299 --> 00:06:59.666
Fascinating. So this town has an ample supply of electrical energy.

123
00:06:59.733 --> 00:07:04.066
In that case, let’s steal every last bit of that energy for ourselves.

124
00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:08.033
Since electricity isn't cheap, we could make a fortune selling it to chumps,

125
00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:10.200
or if we gave it all to the Boss.

126
00:07:10.266 --> 00:07:13.566
- He’d be shocked. But happy.
- Wobbuffet!

127
00:07:19.366 --> 00:07:24.299
Luxio? Lu! Lux!

128
00:07:28.933 --> 00:07:31.400
-That was close one.

129
00:07:31.466 --> 00:07:34.299
Dropping pliers could have been bad for your health.

130
00:07:34.366 --> 00:07:36.900
Wobbo! Wob!

131
00:07:36.966 --> 00:07:40.633
I wonder what that Luxio was doing wandering around here.

132
00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.933
Not sure, but we’d better hurry up.

133
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.366
If you control electricity, you control the world.

134
00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.833
Our ticket to a high-voltage future.

135
00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.400
Right. We can lure Pikachu in using the stolen electricity

136
00:07:53.466 --> 00:07:58.799
and then we’ll catch it. Perfect! And goal! Yay!

137
00:08:02.933 --> 00:08:05.400
- Huh?
- Please excuse us.

138
00:08:05.466 --> 00:08:08.000
This is the system control room I designed myself.

139
00:08:08.066 --> 00:08:10.066
Clemont. What a nice surprise.

140
00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.666
I’m sorry to barge in, but I was wondering,

141
00:08:12.733 --> 00:08:14.400
may I show all my friends around?

142
00:08:14.466 --> 00:08:16.933
Of course. It’s no problem at all.

143
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.299
- Huh?

144
00:08:19.366 --> 00:08:20.366
Status report.

145
00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:24.533
There’s a problem with the transmission cables near the transformer.

146
00:08:24.599 --> 00:08:28.366
- Transformer? That doesn’t sound good.
- Just what are you referring to?

147
00:08:28.433 --> 00:08:33.600
Well, uh, the thing is, a wild Pokémon has been making its home there.

148
00:08:33.666 --> 00:08:35.166
Wild Pokémon?

149
00:08:35.233 --> 00:08:40.566
Yes. When we approach, it attacks. So we’re kind of at a loss.

150
00:08:40.633 --> 00:08:44.466
- It’s okay. I’ll go and have a look.
- Please, let me come with you.

151
00:08:44.533 --> 00:08:47.233
- Yeah. I'll go too.
- Pika. Pika.

152
00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:50.300
Since you’re the designer, we value your opinions.

153
00:08:50.366 --> 00:08:54.033
- Give us some feedback.
- I want you to wait here for me, Bonnie.

154
00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.300
- Will you keep an eye on her?
- Mm-hm. Count on me.

155
00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.000
-It’s at the end of that passageway.

156
00:09:04.066 --> 00:09:05.866
Come on, what's the holdup?

157
00:09:05.933 --> 00:09:08.800
It’s a bit trickier than I thought.

158
00:09:08.866 --> 00:09:11.800
- Hey. Who’s in there?
- Ah! Team Rocket.

159
00:09:11.866 --> 00:09:13.966
- What are you doing here?
- Pika?

160
00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:16.500
I think we’d better make like a tree and leave.

161
00:09:16.566 --> 00:09:19.266
Wobbuff!

162
00:09:19.333 --> 00:09:20.833
Stop!

163
00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.900
- Luxio. Lu!
- Huh?

164
00:09:23.966 --> 00:09:27.133
- What Pokémon is that?
- A Luxio.

165
00:09:30.199 --> 00:09:33.033
Who’s that Pokémon?

166
00:09:36.166 --> 00:09:38.333
It’s Luxio.

167
00:09:44.233 --> 00:09:48.266
Luxio, the Spark Pokémon and the evolved form of Shinx.

168
00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:50.800
Luxio’s sharp claws conduct electricity

169
00:09:50.866 --> 00:09:54.566
and the slightest scratch can knock out an opponent.

170
00:09:54.633 --> 00:09:56.066
Lu!

171
00:09:56.133 --> 00:09:58.266
- Huh?
- Pikachu, Thunderbolt.

172
00:09:58.333 --> 00:10:00.466
Pikachu!

173
00:10:02.033 --> 00:10:03.400
Lu!

174
00:10:03.466 --> 00:10:05.633
Hey, we’re not your enemies! Stop!

175
00:10:05.699 --> 00:10:08.900
You’re looking for the bad guys! They went that way!

176
00:10:08.966 --> 00:10:14.800
- Lux! Lux! Lux! Lux!
- Oh!

177
00:10:14.866 --> 00:10:20.666
- Uh! It’s you!
- Lux. Lux. Lux?

178
00:10:20.733 --> 00:10:23.199
Luxio!

179
00:10:24.966 --> 00:10:27.966
Luxio! Lux. Lux

180
00:10:28.966 --> 00:10:31.433
- Lux. Lux. Lux. Lux.
- Hm?

181
00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:34.633
Just great. It’s that pesky Luxio again.

182
00:10:34.699 --> 00:10:38.699
Oh! That’s what the science twerp was talking about.

183
00:10:39.933 --> 00:10:43.433
It looks like we just might have to rethink our strategy.

184
00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.233
We’ll retool, then send the twerps back to Team Rocket school.

185
00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:48.733
Wobbuffet!

186
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:50.300
Team Rocket?

187
00:10:50.366 --> 00:10:55.066
They’re really bad guys who like to steal other people’s stuff and Pokémon, too.

188
00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:56.100
Pikachu!

189
00:10:56.166 --> 00:10:58.666
So they want to steal the town’s electricity.

190
00:10:58.733 --> 00:11:01.800
- Then we’re going to have to stop them.
- They’re stubborn.

191
00:11:01.866 --> 00:11:04.633
- I’m sure they’ll be back.
- That’s for sure.

192
00:11:04.699 --> 00:11:09.400
They’ve caused an awful lot of trouble for us in the past. Right, Clemont?

193
00:11:10.833 --> 00:11:12.833
- Clemont, wake up!
- Huh?

194
00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.600
Yes, right. They’re troublemakers.

195
00:11:15.666 --> 00:11:21.000
- Well, we need to come up with a plan.
- We'll have to be on full alert.

196
00:11:21.066 --> 00:11:23.600
I’ll let Officer Jenny know what’s going on.

197
00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.333
There. All pretty now.

198
00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:36.400
Cha! Ah!

199
00:11:36.466 --> 00:11:39.566
- Okay, Fennekin, you’re next.
- Fennekin!

200
00:11:41.466 --> 00:11:45.133
- Clemont, what’s bothering you?
- Na-na-na?

201
00:11:45.199 --> 00:11:48.500
Uh, well, I was just thinking about Shinx.

202
00:11:48.566 --> 00:11:52.666
Oh, Shinx. You mean that Pokémon that you helped when you went to school here?

203
00:11:52.733 --> 00:11:56.166
- It’s probably still here in this town.
- Pika.

204
00:11:56.233 --> 00:11:58.166
- I’m sure of it.
- Huh?

205
00:11:58.233 --> 00:12:01.000
I never finished the story I told you.

206
00:12:01.066 --> 00:12:04.966
It was the day before my graduation. Something bad happened.

207
00:12:05.966 --> 00:12:08.133
Shinx and I had a regular meeting place.

208
00:12:08.199 --> 00:12:10.266
I was on my way to thank Shinx for the idea

209
00:12:10.333 --> 00:12:12.199
that led me to my graduation research.

210
00:12:12.266 --> 00:12:15.066
This cake is decorated with lots of berries

211
00:12:15.133 --> 00:12:17.500
for just the right amount of sweetness.

212
00:12:17.566 --> 00:12:20.199
There’s no doubt Shinx is going to adore it.

213
00:12:21.633 --> 00:12:24.199
Then I’ll ask Shinx to become my partner

214
00:12:24.266 --> 00:12:27.733
and travel along with me back to Lumiose City.

215
00:12:29.699 --> 00:12:32.533
- Oh, it’s Clemont.
- Hello, Mr. Mayor.

216
00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:36.099
I’ve been looking all over for you and here you are.

217
00:12:36.166 --> 00:12:38.766
We’ve arranged a very special dinner for you

218
00:12:38.833 --> 00:12:41.833
to help celebrate your graduation. Please, get in.

219
00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.666
But, Mr. Mayor--

220
00:12:43.733 --> 00:12:48.433
Quick. The whole town is waiting for you at the restaurant. Time’s a-wasting.

221
00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:53.599
- Come on, let’s go.
- But... But, Mr. Mayor!

222
00:12:54.599 --> 00:12:56.266
All right.

223
00:12:58.966 --> 00:13:03.033
Oh! Shinx!

224
00:13:06.866 --> 00:13:10.099
As soon as I could, I hurried back there after dinner,

225
00:13:10.166 --> 00:13:12.466
but Shinx wasn’t anywhere to be found.

226
00:13:12.533 --> 00:13:15.033
And after that, I never saw Shinx again.

227
00:13:15.099 --> 00:13:16.766
I get it.

228
00:13:16.833 --> 00:13:20.333
Hey. When Shinx evolves, it becomes Luxio, right?

229
00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.766
So could that Luxio possibly be...?

230
00:13:22.833 --> 00:13:24.833
- Na-na-na?
- Luxio? It evolved?

231
00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.500
Maybe it evolved from the Shinx that was your friend.

232
00:13:27.566 --> 00:13:29.466
Well, maybe I’m wrong.

233
00:13:29.533 --> 00:13:33.566
Remember, that Luxio didn’t even respond to you, Clemont.

234
00:13:33.633 --> 00:13:36.766
No. Your hypothesis is probably correct.

235
00:13:36.833 --> 00:13:40.666
- Huh?
- Yeah. Looking in Luxio’s eyes!

236
00:13:44.599 --> 00:13:47.066
No doubt. It’s the same Pokémon.

237
00:13:47.133 --> 00:13:50.199
That Luxio has to be my friend Shinx after it evolved!

238
00:13:50.266 --> 00:13:52.300
- No way.
- Pika!

239
00:13:52.366 --> 00:13:56.366
I never showed up at our meeting place that day like I promised.

240
00:13:56.433 --> 00:13:59.566
So Shinx must have thought I abandoned it.

241
00:13:59.633 --> 00:14:01.666
That’s why.

242
00:14:03.033 --> 00:14:04.500
Hm. Huh?

243
00:14:04.566 --> 00:14:06.566
- Oh, no, it’s a blackout.
- Pika!

244
00:14:06.633 --> 00:14:08.599
Clemont, this is awful!

245
00:14:08.666 --> 00:14:11.300
A huge amount of electricity has been drained from the system!

246
00:14:11.366 --> 00:14:13.866
-I’ll bet it’s Team Rocket again.

247
00:14:13.933 --> 00:14:15.500
Pika! Pika!

248
00:14:19.233 --> 00:14:22.400
Luxio? Lux?

249
00:14:23.266 --> 00:14:24.900
Lux! Lux! Lux! Lux!

250
00:14:28.933 --> 00:14:31.833
There’s nothing like getting electricity at no cost.

251
00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.000
And what could be freer than free?

252
00:14:34.066 --> 00:14:35.400
Wobbuffet!

253
00:14:35.466 --> 00:14:38.400
-Lux!

254
00:14:39.699 --> 00:14:40.699
Lux!

255
00:14:40.766 --> 00:14:44.699
- Why, you little pest!
- We’ve had about enough of you.

256
00:14:44.766 --> 00:14:47.166
And that’s your cue, Pumpkaboo!

257
00:14:48.966 --> 00:14:50.300
Pumpkaboo!

258
00:14:50.366 --> 00:14:52.833
Inkay, you too.

259
00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.166
Inkay!

260
00:14:54.233 --> 00:14:57.366
I told the townspeople that they should stay inside their homes

261
00:14:57.433 --> 00:14:59.166
until this whole issue is solved.

262
00:14:59.233 --> 00:15:03.233
Also, according to Officer Jenny, they found no one below ground.

263
00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.233
But where did Team Rocket go?

264
00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:10.133
They were able to drain all of the town’s electricity at once somehow.

265
00:15:10.199 --> 00:15:11.466
Hey, I’ve got it.

266
00:15:11.533 --> 00:15:14.633
- Pumpkaboo!
- Inkay!

267
00:15:14.699 --> 00:15:17.900
Shadow Ball!

268
00:15:17.966 --> 00:15:20.500
Lux!

269
00:15:22.833 --> 00:15:24.733
Luxio!

270
00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.800
Team Rocket, there you are!

271
00:15:26.866 --> 00:15:29.533
We won’t allow you to steal any more electricity.

272
00:15:29.599 --> 00:15:32.133
Prepare for trouble, how pompous is that?

273
00:15:32.199 --> 00:15:34.533
And make it double, it’s tit for tat.

274
00:15:34.599 --> 00:15:37.033
To protect the world from devastation.

275
00:15:37.099 --> 00:15:39.766
To unite all people within our nation.

276
00:15:39.833 --> 00:15:42.833
To denounce the evils of all your rules.

277
00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:46.566
To shut down the power on arrogant schools.

278
00:15:46.633 --> 00:15:48.733
- Jessie.
- And James.

279
00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:51.599
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

280
00:15:51.666 --> 00:15:54.666
Surrender now, or prepare for a lights-out fight.

281
00:15:54.733 --> 00:15:56.066
Meowth, that’s right!

282
00:15:56.133 --> 00:15:57.800
Wobbuffet!

283
00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:00.599
-Huh?

284
00:16:00.666 --> 00:16:03.800
Lux! Lux!

285
00:16:03.866 --> 00:16:09.000
- No way, Inkay. I call Foul Play!
- Inkay!

286
00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.933
- Pumpkaboo, Shadow Ball.
- Pumpka!

287
00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.300
Pikachu, use Electro Ball.

288
00:16:15.366 --> 00:16:19.400
Pika! Pika! Pika! Pikachu!

289
00:16:21.433 --> 00:16:23.433
-Don’t worry, Luxio.

290
00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.800
Just stay down and we’ll take care of this.

291
00:16:25.866 --> 00:16:26.733
Luxio!

292
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.633
Why do you insist on battling with Team Rocket?

293
00:16:29.699 --> 00:16:33.366
Lux! Luxio! Luxio! Lux! Lux! Lux!

294
00:16:33.433 --> 00:16:37.633
Dig this, Luxio wants a town where all Pokémon can live happily.

295
00:16:37.699 --> 00:16:40.599
It’s protecting the place the science twerp helped change.

296
00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:43.833
Where all Pokémon can live happily? Huh!

297
00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:47.066
I want to help make a town where all Electric-type can live there happily!

298
00:16:47.133 --> 00:16:50.099
No, a world where all Pokémon can live happily.

299
00:16:50.166 --> 00:16:51.833
That would be my dream come true.

300
00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.633
- Ha! Luxio.
- The nerve. How pompous!

301
00:16:54.699 --> 00:16:57.566
Finish this with Shadow Ball.

302
00:16:57.633 --> 00:16:59.366
Look out!

303
00:16:59.433 --> 00:17:00.866
- Luxio!
- Argh!

304
00:17:00.933 --> 00:17:03.666
-Clemont, no!

305
00:17:03.733 --> 00:17:06.666
- Lux!
- Thank goodness you’re okay.

306
00:17:06.733 --> 00:17:09.666
- Hm!
- Lux?

307
00:17:09.733 --> 00:17:12.033
- Shinx!
- Ah!

308
00:17:12.099 --> 00:17:14.433
Shinx? Shinx! Shinx! Shinx!

309
00:17:16.166 --> 00:17:18.733
Shinx! Shinx!

310
00:17:24.399 --> 00:17:27.200
- Shinx!
- Hm!

311
00:17:29.433 --> 00:17:31.399
Luxio!

312
00:17:32.666 --> 00:17:34.666
-Huh?

313
00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:38.600
Huh, Luxio!

314
00:17:38.666 --> 00:17:42.333
We got the juice, so time to cut loose. Now for Pikachu.

315
00:17:42.399 --> 00:17:45.833
- You’re coming with us, without an excuse.
- Wobbuff!

316
00:17:46.966 --> 00:17:51.300
- Okay, Inkay! Use Psybeam!
- Now, Pumpkaboo, Dark Pulse!

317
00:17:51.366 --> 00:17:52.700
- Inkay!
- Pumpka!

318
00:17:52.766 --> 00:17:53.833
Thunderbolt!

319
00:17:53.899 --> 00:17:56.366
Pikachu!

320
00:17:57.433 --> 00:17:58.600
Uh!

321
00:18:00.266 --> 00:18:03.533
Hm! Luxio, would you please stand and battle with me?

322
00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.066
- Lux!
- Huh?

323
00:18:05.133 --> 00:18:07.833
Great. Use Discharge!

324
00:18:07.899 --> 00:18:10.800
Lux!

325
00:18:14.333 --> 00:18:16.033
School’s out!

326
00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:18.633
We’re blasting off again!

327
00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.233
- Wobbuffet!
- Inkay!

328
00:18:22.399 --> 00:18:26.333
We did it. We did it. We did it. Yay!

329
00:18:31.899 --> 00:18:34.899
Luxio.

330
00:18:35.899 --> 00:18:37.899
Please, wait.

331
00:18:40.533 --> 00:18:43.566
Luxio, I’d really like you to come with me.

332
00:18:47.466 --> 00:18:51.866
I remember. I gave you my word, then let you down.

333
00:18:52.866 --> 00:18:55.800
But now I’ll be waiting for you,

334
00:18:55.866 --> 00:18:58.633
at the same place and at the exact same time.

335
00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:04.433
So if you decide to come with me, meet me in the square.

336
00:19:08.133 --> 00:19:09.166
Hm.

337
00:19:22.399 --> 00:19:24.433
I don’t see Luxio anywhere.

338
00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:28.600
- I guess that means it’s still mad.
- Na-na!

339
00:19:28.666 --> 00:19:32.399
Luxio will show up. We’ve got to give it a little more time.

340
00:19:32.466 --> 00:19:33.833
Pika!

341
00:19:33.899 --> 00:19:35.833
- No.
- Huh?

342
00:19:35.899 --> 00:19:40.300
I guess that Luxio still hasn’t forgiven me, which is all that I deserve.

343
00:19:40.366 --> 00:19:43.866
It’s time to go. If I stay here any longer,

344
00:19:43.933 --> 00:19:46.233
it won’t be fair to the rest of you.

345
00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:49.200
Hm. Let’s get back on the road.

346
00:19:51.833 --> 00:19:53.833
Huh?

347
00:19:58.133 --> 00:20:03.800
Huh? Hm!

348
00:20:03.866 --> 00:20:07.566
You came back after all. Luxio!

349
00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.566
Lux!

350
00:20:11.633 --> 00:20:16.033
Wow! Okay, here goes. Go, Poké Ball!

351
00:20:21.866 --> 00:20:25.233
All right. Today’s a great day, thanks to science.

352
00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:28.433
- I caught Luxio!
- Yay. That’s my big brother!

353
00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.333
- All right!
- Pika!

354
00:20:31.399 --> 00:20:34.866
Thank you, Luxio. I won’t let you down.

355
00:20:34.933 --> 00:20:37.500
And so, two old friends reunite,

356
00:20:37.566 --> 00:20:41.066
as Luxio becomes the newest member of our heroes’ family.

357
00:20:41.133 --> 00:20:44.866
But their quest to meet new people and new Pokémon will go on,

358
00:20:44.933 --> 00:20:47.399
as the journey continues...
